---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Spidergraph — Breach Check Tracker"
  description="Track your own quarterly Have I Been Pwned checks across every email/alias you use — a self-managed local checklist, no lookups performed here."
  path="breach-check-tracker/"
  current="breach-check"
  accent="blue"
>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}shared/tool-page.css`} />
  <link
    slot="head"
    rel="stylesheet"
    href={`${base}pages/breach-check-tracker.css`}
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">
          Self-audit · <span id="itemCount">0</span> addresses tracked
        </div>
        <h1>
          Breach <span>Check Tracker</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="sub">
          List every email address and alias you actually use, then check each
          one on Have I Been Pwned yourself once a quarter. This page never
          looks anything up for you — it only remembers which addresses you've
          checked and when.
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="reset-btn" id="resetBtn">
        Reset tracker
      </button>
    </header>

    <div class="intro-card">
      <b>Why this exists:</b> Domain 1 and Domain 8 of the Playbook both
      recommend a Have I Been Pwned check as a free, do-this-first step — but
      until now nothing on this site made that a trackable habit the way the
      Broker Removal Tracker does for opt-outs. This tool deliberately does{' '}
      <b>not</b> query any breach database itself: it would need a backend and
      your email to do that server-side, which is exactly the kind of feature
      Spidergraph's own scope rules out (see the Playbook, or CONTRIBUTING.md if
      you're a contributor). Instead, add your own addresses below, click
      through to Have I Been Pwned to check each one yourself, and tick it off —
      same shape as the rest of this site: you provide the input, you do the
      verification, this page just remembers your progress.
      <div class="links">
        <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          🔍 Open Have I Been Pwned →
        </a>
        <a href="../playbook/#8-osint-digital-footprint">
          📖 Read Domain 8 in the Playbook →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="layout">
      <div>
        <div class="list-head">
          <span class="list-head-title">Your addresses</span>
        </div>

        <div class="add-row">
          <input
            type="text"
            id="addrInput"
            placeholder="you@example.com or an alias label"
            aria-label="Email address or alias to track"
            maxlength="120"
          />
          <button type="button" id="addBtn">
            Add
          </button>
        </div>

        <div id="emptyState" class="empty-state" hidden>
          Nothing tracked yet — add an email address or alias above to start
          your quarterly Have I Been Pwned habit.
        </div>
        <div id="addrList"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Progress</div>
          <div class="score-row">
            <div>
              <div class="score-num" id="scoreNum">
                0%
              </div>
              <div class="score-label">checked this cycle</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Summary</div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Checked</span>
            <span class="v teal" id="mDone">
              0/0
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Not checked</span>
            <span class="v amber" id="mTodo">
              0
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Companion tool</div>
          <p class="small">
            This tracks your own addresses. If it's a listing on a people-search
            site instead of a breach, that's the Broker Removal Tracker's job,
            not this one.
          </p>
          <a class="card-link" href="../broker-removal-tracker/">
            Broker Removal Tracker →
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Export</div>
          <button type="button" id="exportBtn" class="reset-btn">
            Export progress ↓
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">History</div>
          <p class="small">
            Save a dated checkpoint to compare your progress over time.
          </p>
          <button
            type="button"
            id="snapshotBtn"
            class="reset-btn"
            style="width:100%; margin-bottom:12px;"
          >
            Save snapshot
          </button>
          <div id="historyList" class="history-list"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer>
      <b>Companion pages:</b> the "why" behind this habit lives in Domains 1 and
      8 of the <b>Playbook</b>. Your address list and checked/unchecked state
      stay in this browser only, in <code>localStorage</code> — nothing is sent
      anywhere, and this page never transmits an address you enter to Have I
      Been Pwned or anywhere else; it only opens a link you click yourself.{' '}
      <b>Reset tracker</b> clears everything.
    </footer>
  </div>

  <script src={`${base}shared/persist.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}shared/history.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}pages/breach-check-tracker.js`} is:inline></script>
</BaseLayout>
